.DS_Store
.envrc
.env*
!.env.enc
!.env.example

# Raw fetch payloads are reproducible via scripts/ and pruned after 28 days —
# never committed. Both trees are covered so the data/sources -> data/raw rename
# cannot leak payloads, and ALL extensions are covered (the old .json-only rule
# was committing .rss/.xml/.jsonl payloads — ~19MB/day once ingest runs hourly).
# The per-run manifest stays: it is the human-readable record of what each fetch did.
# Level 1 catches stray files written straight into the tree (runner logs);
# the !*/ rules keep the dated directories traversable so the manifest survives.
data/sources/*
data/raw/*
!data/sources/*/
!data/raw/*/
data/sources/*/*
data/raw/*/*
!data/sources/*/manifest.md
!data/raw/*/manifest.md

# The working store: deterministically rebuildable from the committed ledgers.
data/register.db
data/register.db-wal
data/register.db-shm
